claimed: nio-port-scope — (a) move okay-http's socket suites to integrationTest with the Live tag, as netty was moved (operator instruction); (b) the timing, continued: TestNio's "the port is free after the scope" does not fail because the OS is slow to release the port, it fails because the port RETURNS TO THE EPHEMERAL POOL and a sibling test under matrix load binds it, so our connect reaches someone else's listener and the assertion inverts. That is unassertable on a shared machine. Nio.listen's Resource value IS the ServerSocketChannel, so the same claim is checkable deterministically through isOpen; fix the assertion rather than only hiding the suite.
